# Cargo build output — `target/` at any depth (the workspace root plus any
# stale per-crate dirs from before the crates were unified into a workspace).
target/

# Locally installed CLI (cargo install --path cli --root .)
/bin/

# NOTE: gobind/capy_core.wasm is a build artefact, but it is COMMITTED on
# purpose and must not be added here. The Go module system cannot run a build
# step, so `go get github.com/olivierdevelops/capy/rust/gobind` can only work if
# the engine the package //go:embeds is already in the tree. Ignoring it makes
# the binding uninstallable by anyone who is not building the Rust workspace
# locally. Regenerate it with gobind/build.sh, which also refuses to commit a
# wasm that disagrees with the current sources.

# Scratch binaries from the devtools comparison scripts.
gobind/smokebin
gobind/benchbin

# A workspace member must not carry its own lockfile; the workspace root
# lockfile (rust/Cargo.lock) is authoritative and cargo ignores this one.
*/Cargo.lock
